Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 06:41:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] bebbossh: only flush the argument line from stdin if it
 is a console

connectClient() always did FGetC(stdin); fflush(stdin) to drop the
argument line that RunCommand() injects into the input handle's buffer.
On a redirected file (bebbossh ... <file) Flush() returns the unread
buffer by seeking back - over the injected argument line, i.e. before
the start of the file. FFS refuses that; the OS 3.2 RAM handler
(ram-handler 47.57) accepts it and delivers ~70 bytes of foreign memory
in front of the data, so uploads from RAM: arrived with garbage.

Only do it if stdin is interactive.

Tested on a Vampire V4SA: uploads from RAM: (1000 B, 1 MiB) and Work:
byte-identical, interactive start unchanged (no argument line as input).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012seUKBRfgcTt43vbc21K3j
---
 src/client.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/client.cpp b/src/client.cpp
index 2418a3e..5afc68d 100644
--- a/src/client.cpp
+++ b/src/client.cpp
@@ -1189,8 +1189,13 @@ bool connectClient() {
 
 #ifdef __AMIGA__
 	// see DOS RKRM: converted to a buffered stream before flushing!
-	FGetC(stdin);
-	fflush(stdin);
+	// Only for a console: on a redirected file (bebbossh ... <file) Flush()
+	// seeks back over the injected argument line, i.e. before the start of
+	// the file - FFS refuses that, RAM: delivers foreign memory instead.
+	if (IsInteractive(stdin) == DOSTRUE) {
+		FGetC(stdin);
+		fflush(stdin);
+	}
 
 	if (escape && !theWindow) {
 		theWindow = IntuitionBase->ActiveWindow;
